    <!-- Guidelines -->
    <string name="guidelines_title">Print Guidelines</string>
    <string name="heading_formats">1. Accepted File Formats</string>
    <string name="desc_formats">We accept the following formats for printing:\n• JPG/JPEG — recommended for photos and raster graphics.\n• PNG — recommended for designs requiring transparent backgrounds.\n• PDF — best for vector graphics and multi-page layouts.</string>
    <string name="heading_resolution">2. Recommended Resolution</string>
    <string name="desc_resolution">To avoid pixelated and blurry prints, verify resolution settings:\n• Standard Print Quality: Minimum 300 DPI.\n• Screen/Draft Quality: 72 DPI (might look blurry in print).</string>
    <string name="heading_color">3. Color Mode</string>
    <string name="desc_color">Use CMYK color mode for designing print artwork. Designing in RGB is acceptable, but automatic conversion to CMYK might result in slight color variations.</string>
    <string name="heading_bleed">4. Bleed and Safe Zone</string>
    <string name="desc_bleed">• Bleed Area: Add 3mm bleed margin around your designs to avoid white lines after cutting.\n• Safe Zone: Keep critical text and details 5mm away from the edge.</string>
    <string name="heading_file_limit">5. File Size Limit</string>
    <string name="desc_file_limit">The maximum file size limit is 20MB. For larger vector illustrations or multi-page formats, compress files to PDF or PNG formats.</string>

